<http://data.silknow.org/object/0a23c6cd-2501-3fe6-ad63-bcdd7dd89fff/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Ground of brocade woven with red and white silk and metal yarns of three types. Formal, symmetrical pattern showing sun faces and bees surrounded by conventionalized leaves and blossoms. Panels bordered with gold galloon. Central panel shows a silver and gold monstrance rendered in laid work; end panels show Barberini arms over Cross of Malta surmounted by cardinal's hat, rendered similarly. Ground worn, metals tarnished; gold laid work still bright. At left and right upper corners, hanging cords of red silk and gold yarns."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0a23c6cd-2501-3fe6-ad63-bcdd7dd89fff> .

